Here are more vulnerabilities (411–420) that sometimes receive bug-bounty rewards when they expose real security risks. Many researchers report them through programs on HackerOne, Bugcrowd, and Intigriti.
More Vulnerabilities That Can Be Paid (411–420)
411. Improper API Authentication
API Authentication Bypass
APIs fail to properly verify authentication tokens or credentials.
💰 Typical payout: $500 – $9,000
412. Insecure Data Serialization Format
Serialization Format Vulnerability
Improper serialization formats allow attackers to manipulate data structures.
💰 Typical payout: $400 – $7,000
413. Improper Validation of File Types
File Type Validation Vulnerability
Applications rely only on file extensions when validating uploads.
💰 Typical payout: $300 – $6,000
414. Insecure Backup Storage
Backup Storage Exposure
Backups stored in publicly accessible locations or weakly protected storage.
💰 Typical payout: $300 – $6,000
415. Improper Session Regeneration
Session Fixation Vulnerability
Session IDs are not regenerated after login, allowing attackers to reuse them.
💰 Typical payout: $500 – $8,000
416. Weak API Authentication Tokens
Weak Authentication Token Generation
Authentication tokens generated with predictable patterns.
💰 Typical payout: $400 – $7,000
417. Unsecured Development Tools in Production
Development Tool Exposure
Developer tools or debug consoles remain accessible in production environments.
💰 Typical payout: $300 – $5,000
418. Improper HTTP Cache Handling
HTTP Cache Misconfiguration
Sensitive responses cached and accessible to other users.
💰 Typical payout: $200 – $4,000
419. Improper Validation of JSON Input
JSON Input Validation Vulnerability
JSON payloads processed without proper validation.
💰 Typical payout: $300 – $5,000
420. Insecure Third-Party API Integration
Third‑Party API Integration Vulnerability
Applications trust external APIs without verifying responses or authenticity.
💰 Typical payout: $400 – $7,000
✅ Important bug-bounty insight
Even though there are 420+ vulnerability types, most big payouts usually come from:
SQL Injection
Cross‑Site Scripting
Server‑Side Request Forgery
Broken Access Control
Remote Code Execution
These can sometimes reach $10,000 – $100,000+ depending on the company.
